README.1ST

  If you are having problems setting up BiModem with Telix & the ATI modem,
  this package may help you.

  If you're just interested in setting up BiModem with Telix then don't run
  the batch files included or change any configuration parameters except for
  the external protocol or set up a function key to call up BIMOD.BAT.	You
  will only need to change the BiModem configuration's RTS/CTS to N.



  README.1ST      -  Take a guess!

  BITLXMNP.DOC    -  The DOCS

  BIPATH.LST      -  Sample list of directories for BiModem to search
                     for files to be sent from your drives.  You MUST
                     edit it to list your own directories containing
                     paths to where your files will be sent from.

  BIMODEM.CFG     -  Sample BiModem configuration configuration v1.14.

  BIMOD.BAT       -  The automated batch file for calling BiModem up
                     from Telix - You may setup a Fkey to call it up or
                     set it up as an external protocol as described in
                     BITLXMNP.DOC.  Recommended that when you call it up
                     you should use Download (Page Down) so you won't be
                     prompted for file names by Telix or better yet set
                     up a F key to call it up.  The %1 and %2 is the speed
                     and port passed from Telix if you're setting BiModem
                     as an external protocol.

  BIMOD1.BAT      -  Same as BIMOD.BAT but without the %1 & %2 parameter
                     for calling BiModem using a function key.

  TELIX.CNF       -  Sample Telix configuration v 3.11.  The COM port has
                     been set to 2.  If you are using a different COM port
                     you should modify the "port=2" to whatever COM port
                     your modem is set at so Telix won't freeze up when it
                     try to initialize the modem.

  BICONFIG.TXT    -  Documentations on configuring BiModem to work properly
                     with the procedure documented here.

  SETUPV42.BAT    -  Batch file for setting up ATI 2400 etc modem with the
                     v.42 protocol.

                Syntax: SETUPV42 n  | Where n is the COM port your modem
                                    | is connected.  Supported are COMs 1-4.


  SETUP.BAT       -  Batch file for setting up the old non-v42 ATI 2400 etc
                     modem.

                Syntax: SETUP n  | Where n is the COM port your modem
                                 | is connected.  Supported are COMs 1-4.

  AT.COM          -  The program needed for SETUP.BAT & SETUPV42.BAT.



Please run either SETUP.BAT or SETUPV42.BAT now then print out
BITLXMNP.DOC and BICONFIG.TXT now then proceed to set up
Telix and BiModem.

Let me know if this is any help at all.  My ego wants to know.  Leave me
a message on an IBM or COMM echo if you have anything to say.


Good Luck!

Geoffrey Sy.

